  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with a budget of $2M approved by the executive board. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing ahead of schedule. The team has expanded to include experts in machine learning and cloud computing. Recent updates highlight a breakthrough in predictive analytics, planned UI enhancements starting in October, and upcoming security protocol updates effective next January. A staff meeting on November 20th will feature a detailed report on phase two progress."
